---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';

// Every cell is a checkable fact. Third-party cells cite the upstream
// repository at the SHA/date in the table note; update the date when editing.
const asOf = '2026-09-30';

const rows = [
  {
    area: 'Origin',
    hornero: 'Extracted in 2026-09 from ulises-jeremias/dotfiles (pin b26db04) into the HorneroOS organisation',
    ryoku: 'Alpha series was a fork of Omarchy; rebuilt from an empty root from the beta series on (per its README)',
    omarchy: 'Arch Linux + Hyprland distribution by DHH; repository created 2025-06',
  },
  {
    area: 'License',
    hornero: 'Shell runtime GPL-3.0-only; composition and config repositories MIT',
    ryoku: 'GPL-3.0',
    omarchy: 'MIT',
  },
  {
    area: 'System CLI',
    hornero: 'horneroctl (18 top-level commands, e.g. appearance, shell, config, doctor)',
    ryoku: 'ryoku CLI; ryoku update takes a snapshot before and after each update',
    omarchy: 'omarchy CLI command center plus omarchy-* scripts in bin/ (e.g. omarchy-update, omarchy-theme-set)',
  },
  {
    area: 'Shell',
    hornero: 'Quickshell shell adapted from Caelestia, 15 layout presets',
    ryoku: 'Quickshell-based Ryoku shell (frame rendering adapted from Caelestia)',
    omarchy: 'Quickshell-based Omarchy shell (bar, menu, notifications, OSD, lock)',
  },
  {
    area: 'Themes',
    hornero: '15 theme packs defined as JSON tokens in HorneroOS/config',
    ryoku: 'Bar, widgets and frame retinted live from the wallpaper',
    omarchy: '22 theme directories in themes/, applied with omarchy-theme-set',
  },
  {
    area: 'Delivery',
    hornero:
      '12 pinned composition manifests (v0.1.0-draft to v0.2.0-preview12); AUR horneroctl-bin at 0.2.0_preview2; no ISO or installer yet',
    ryoku: 'Signed ISO and signed [ryoku] pacman repository',
    omarchy: 'ISO download from omarchy.org',
  },
  {
    area: 'Compositors',
    hornero: 'Hyprland only',
    ryoku: 'Hyprland or niri',
    omarchy: 'Hyprland',
  },
];
---

<SiteLayout title="Roots — Hornero OS" description="Where Hornero OS comes from, what it credits, and how it compares.">
  <section class="section">
    <h1>Roots</h1>
    <p>
      HorneroOS grew out of the <a href="https://github.com/ulises-jeremias/dotfiles">ulises-jeremias/dotfiles</a>{' '}
      repository. In September 2026 its Quickshell desktop and configuration were extracted into the HorneroOS
      organisation. While building that desktop, two Quickshell projects were studied closely:{' '}
      <strong>Caelestia</strong> and <strong>DankMaterialShell</strong>.
    </p>
    <p>
      Credits: the Hornero shell adapts <a href="https://github.com/caelestia-dots/shell">caelestia-dots/shell</a>{' '}
      (GPL-3.0), with attribution preserved in{' '}
      <a href="https://github.com/HorneroOS/shell/blob/main/NOTICE">shell/NOTICE</a>. The <code class="inline">horneroctl</code> CLI, the config packs, the greeter, the installer contract and the
      release manifests are written in the HorneroOS repositories.
    </p>
    <p>
      HorneroOS is not a fork of Omarchy: the shell was imported from the dotfiles repository, and the import record is
      in <code class="inline">shell/NOTICE</code>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2 id="compare-heading">How it compares</h2>
    <p>
      HorneroOS side by side with two other Arch Linux desktops built on Hyprland:{' '}
      <a href="https://github.com/Ryoku-dev/ryoku">Ryoku</a> and{' '}
      <a href="https://github.com/omacom/omarchy">Omarchy</a>. Third-party facts come from each project&apos;s own repository. Corrections are welcome as{' '}
      <a href="https://github.com/HorneroOS/website/issues">website issues</a>.
    </p>
    <div class="table-scroll" role="region" aria-labelledby="compare-heading" tabindex="0">
      <table class="compare">
        <caption>HorneroOS, Ryoku and Omarchy compared</caption>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col">Area</th>
            <th scope="col">HorneroOS</th>
            <th scope="col">Ryoku</th>
            <th scope="col">Omarchy</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {rows.map((r) => (
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">{r.area}</th>
              <td>{r.hornero}</td>
              <td>{r.ryoku}</td>
              <td>{r.omarchy}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="table-note">
      Facts as of {asOf}. Sources: HorneroOS repositories; Ryoku README at{' '}
      <a href="https://github.com/Ryoku-dev/ryoku/tree/98a0368">98a0368</a>{' '}
      (2026-09-26); Omarchy repository at{' '}
      <a href="https://github.com/omacom/omarchy/tree/8b4eae6">8b4eae6</a>{' '}
      (2026-09-29).
    </p>
    <p>
      Ideas taken from Ryoku are tracked as public issues, for example{' '}
      <a href="https://github.com/HorneroOS/hornero/issues/62">hornero#62</a> (update, rollback and snapshot lanes).
    </p>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
